      "payload": {
        "chunks": [
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "CPChem has two major integrated polymer projects under construction, the Golden Triangle Polymers Project in Orange, Texas, for which CPChem holds a 51 percent-owned and operated interest and the Ras Laffan Petrochemical Project in Ras Laffan, Qatar, for which CPChem holds a 30 percent nonoperated working interest. Start-up for both projects is targeted for 2026.",
            "entity_name": "CPChem Golden Triangle Polymers Project",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "CPChem has two major integrated polymer projects under construction, the Golden Triangle Polymers Project in Orange, Texas, for which CPChem holds a 51 percent-owned and operated interest and the Ras Laffan Petrochemical Project in Ras Laffan, Qatar, for which CPChem holds a 30 percent nonoperated working interest. Start-up for both projects is targeted for 2026.",
            "entity_name": "CPChem Ras Laffan Petrochemical Project",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In California, commercial operations began in 2024 at the central gas processing facility for CalBioGas Hilmar LLC, the company's newest partnership with California Bioenergy LLC, which includes seven new anaerobic digestion dairy farm projects.",
            "entity_name": "CVX CalBioGas Hilmar LLC Partnership Commercial Operations 2024",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "Chevron holds a 50 percent working interest in Bunge Chevron Ag Renewables LLC, which produces soybean oil from processing facilities in Destrehan, Louisiana, and Cairo, Illinois. Soybean oil can be used as a renewable feedstock to make renewable diesel, biodiesel and sustainable aviation fuel. In 2024, FID was taken to build a new oilseed processing plant in Louisiana.",
            "entity_name": "Bunge Chevron Ag Renewables Louisiana Oilseed Plant FID 2024",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "esg_commitment",
            "content": "Expansion work at the Geismar renewable diesel plant in Louisiana to increase production capacity from 7,000 to 22,000 barrels per day is in final commissioning stage, with startup expected in first quarter 2025.",
            "entity_name": "CVX Geismar Renewable Diesel Capacity Expansion",
            "entity_type_entity": "ESGCommitment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "esg_commitment",
            "content": "In 2024, Chevron announced plans to install a hard-sail wind-assisted propulsion system on a new time-chartered LNG carrier to reduce carbon intensity, with an expected delivery in 2026.",
            "entity_name": "CVX LNG Carrier Wind-Assisted Propulsion System",
            "entity_type_entity": "ESGCommitment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "esg_commitment",
            "content": "The new energies organization is focused on developing new businesses with the aim to support the company's objectives to lower the carbon intensity of its operations and enable growth opportunities with the potential to generate competitive returns. These include additional fuel solutions utilizing hydrogen and its derivatives such as ammonia, carbon emissions management through carbon capture and offsets, and power generation for data centers.",
            "entity_name": "CVX New Energies Carbon Intensity Reduction Program",
            "entity_type_entity": "ESGCommitment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          }
        ],
